<title>USA: Reebok accepts 17 mln shrs in self tender.</title>
<headline>Reebok accepts 17 mln shrs in self tender.</headline>
<dateline>STOUGHTON, Mass 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reebok International Ltd said Tuesday a preliminary count of its &quot;Dutch auction&quot; self-tender offer showed 17,018,090 common shares had been accepted for purchase at $36.00 per share.  </p>
<p>Reebok said the tender offer will reduce the number of outstanding common shares to 55,518,610 from 72,536,700.</p>
<p>CS First Boston acted as the dealer manager for the tender offer, it added.</p>
<p>The sports footwear maker said it would use senior bank financing underwritten by Credit Suisse to buy the shares.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
